    "user_request_original": "Perform one bounded TMM thickness optimization for an exactly 7-layer planar stack. Use the fixed material sequence from the incident side: Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr. Optimize only the physical thickness of each finite layer within the user-declared bounds. Do not optimize material identity or layer count in this route. Optimize a 7-layer planar multilayer stack on Al substrate with material sequence Cr/HfO2/SiO2/Cr/HfO2/SiO2/Cr at normal incidence. All 7 finite layers have independent thickness variables bounded [15, 90] nm. Use L-BFGS-B optimizer with hard post-step clipping enforcing min 15nm and max 90nm. Apply quadratic penalty when total thickness deviates from 400nm target. Evaluate mean absorptance in 400-700nm band and mean reflectance in 700-2000nm band. Initialize with 50nm uniform thickness for all layers. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
